<title>CHINA: Shanghai Sewing Machine buys factory.</title>
<headline>Shanghai Sewing Machine buys factory.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shanghai Sewing Machine plans to take over the Shanghai No.2 Electric Appliance Factory, a bankrupt firm, for the price of 17 million yuan, the company said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Shanghai Sewing Machine does not have to take responsibility for the factory's debts but must make arrangements for its 381 staff, the statement said.</p>
<p>The Shanghai No.2 Electric Appliance Factory has net assets of 18.782 million yuan, including 10,733 square metres of land, after being declared bankrupt on November 21, it said. ($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
